          <p>Elmhurst brick spans 1910s Prairie-style lime mortar homes to 1960s colonials built with Type S/N Portland blends. The correct tuckpointing approach differs completely between these eras — wrong mortar causes moisture trapping that destroys the brick face. We identify building era and test original mortar before prescribing any mix in zip code {zipCodes}, DuPage County.</p>
          <p>Prairie-era homes need lime putty mortar; mid-century colonials need Portland-lime blends. We don't guess — we assess first and match to the original. Free estimates, written scope, era-appropriate mortar for every Elmhurst decade.</p>
